{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"wellknown-irrational-aoudad","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context\nChild of epic 5c34-4343-a3e6-4ad5; follows task c3fc-4398-cdd2-4d37 (taxonomy/matrix). Phase 3+4: candidate questions, scoring, selection of the 10, and Kehoe-persona validation.\n\n## Plan\nDraft ~25 candidate questions from the highest-severity assumed/unknown gap-matrix cells. Score each on: risk-reduction leverage; answerability in discovery (names a specific obtainable artifact — e.g. current ACES ICD, WAHBE MOU, contraction budget model, Deloitte M&O contract, TSB decision record); and whether the answer changes a decision-model input (pain/coupling/change/write-back/contract pins). Show the rubric; keep the full candidate table in Appendix B. Select exactly 10; each carries: failure mode de-risked (corpus citation), the specific WA gap, the artifact to request, and answer-to-plan mapping. Validate: run the 10 past the Kehoe persona via a new harness `evaluations/virtual-cio/wa-discovery-questions-review/run-eval.mjs` (adapted from evaluation-wa-report/run-eval.mjs; Bedrock us-east-1 sonnet-class, profile evaluations/virtual-cio/profiles/wa.md), asking whether the questions are credible, answerable, and confidence-building (not audit-flavored) from the buyer's seat. Keep raw request/response in wa-discovery-questions-review/raw/; write findings.md; revise questions per findings and note what changed. Trace-check: every question cites >=1 corpus failure instance and >=1 specific WA gap.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exactly 10 questions: `test \"$(grep -c '^### Q' docs/analysis/wa-discovery-questions-2026-08.md)\" -eq 10`\n- [ ] Scoring rubric + candidate appendix present: `grep -q 'Scoring rubric' docs/analysis/wa-discovery-questions-2026-08.md && grep -q '^## Appendix B — candidate questions' docs/analysis/wa-discovery-questions-2026-08.md`\n- [ ] Every question carries the four required fields: `test \"$(grep -c '^- \\*\\*De-risks' docs/analysis/wa-discovery-questions-2026-08.md)\" -eq 10 && test \"$(grep -c '^- \\*\\*Why WA' docs/analysis/wa-discovery-questions-2026-08.md)\" -eq 10 && test \"$(grep -c '^- \\*\\*Ask for' docs/analysis/wa-discovery-questions-2026-08.md)\" -eq 10 && test \"$(grep -c '^- \\*\\*How the answer moves the plan' docs/analysis/wa-discovery-questions-2026-08.md)\" -eq 10`\n- [ ] Persona-validation raw artifacts committed: `ls evaluations/virtual-cio/wa-discovery-questions-review/raw/*request*.json && ls evaluations/virtual-cio/wa-discovery-questions-review/raw/*response*.json`\n- [ ] Validation findings + post-validation revision note committed: `test -f evaluations/virtual-cio/wa-discovery-questions-review/findings.md && grep -q 'What changed after validation' docs/analysis/wa-discovery-questions-2026-08.md`\n\n## Testing\nDeterministic grep/test/ls commands above from repo root on branch feat/wa-discovery-questions. The Bedrock run itself is external; its committed raw request/response JSON is the durable proof (no secrets in artifacts). Docs+evaluations only; no app build.","id":"2cde-38f5-1744-40fc","parent_id":"5c34-4343-a3e6-4ad5","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Drafting, scoring, selecting, and persona-validating the 10 WA discovery questions"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787967419661882918,"uuid":"8123ee5a-dc06-41db-b0dc-4809b4d13bb8"}